# demand_beside_recursion_1 oracle sidecar: mirrors demand_beside_recursion_1.main.cpp
# exactly (the oracle sees the PLAIN program -- no demand -- and referees
# ANSWER-identity: its final pair/pair_of rows are the full materialization
# the demand-pruned driver answers key-by-key, and its path/path_out rows are
# the full beside-recursion closure).
# Batch 1: chain 10->20->30, detached edge 40->50; four seeds.
# Batch 2: extend chain (30->60), close cycle (50->40); two more seeds.
batch
+ edge_2 10 20
+ edge_2 20 30
+ edge_2 40 50
+ seed_2 1 100
+ seed_2 1 101
+ seed_2 2 200
+ seed_2 3 300
end
batch
+ edge_2 30 60
+ edge_2 50 40
+ seed_2 3 301
+ seed_2 5 500
end
